# Assert.Arg count parameters + multiple independent Assert.Arg lines. Each
# line is its own assert with its own names and (count) parameters: a bare
# number means "exactly this many" of the listed names, and > >= < <= prefixes
# give the other comparisons; several parameters space-separated must all hold.
# The asserts are gated behind the 'check' option so a plain build succeeds.
#
# Extra invocations:
#   riftbuild check a d e f     -> must succeed (every line satisfied)
#   riftbuild check a c d e f   -> must FAIL (both 'a' and 'c' given, exactly one allowed)
#   riftbuild check a e f       -> must FAIL ('d' missing)
#   riftbuild check a d         -> must FAIL (none of 'e' 'f' 'g', needs two or three)
Assembly    AssertArgs
SourceFiles main

option.check Enables the Assert.Arg checks for this test.

Assert.Arg:check                    # valueless form: at least one argument of any kind ('check' itself counts)
Assert.Arg(=1):check     a c        # exactly one of these
Assert.Arg:check         d          # no parameters: every listed name is required
Assert.Arg(>1 <=3):check e f g      # both must hold: two or three of these
